Write a function gcd_plus_ds that takes two unsigned 32-bit numbers a and b and returns gcd(a, b) plus the sum of the decimal digits of a. Write and use a helper function gcd(a, b) that returns the greatest common divisor by repeated remainders (gcd(a, 0) = a, gcd(0, 0) = 0). Write and use a helper function digsum(n) that returns the sum of the decimal digits of n (0 for n = 0). Unsigned 32-bit arithmetic wraps around modulo 2^32 (it never traps).
